# Minutes

This directory holds approved meeting minutes for {{ org_name }}'s Board of
Directors and its committees.

## What belongs here

- Finalized, board-approved minutes for regular, special, and committee
  meetings, using the `MIN-YYYY-QN` identifier scheme described in
  `GOVERNANCE.md`, Section 9.
- Nothing else. Draft minutes, meeting preparation notes, and recordings
  or transcripts that have not yet been approved do not belong in this
  repository at all — see the note on drafting spaces in `CLAUDE.md`.

## How minutes get here

Minutes are drafted, reviewed, and adopted through this repository's
ordinary governance process (see `GOVERNANCE.md`): an officer opens
{{ "an" if vcs_platform == "gitlab" else "a" }} {{ mr_term }} on an `admin/`
branch, the required officer approval is recorded as {{ mr_abbr }}
approval, and the merge to `main` is the adoption event.

## A note on privacy

This directory is a scaffold. It ships empty. Real minutes frequently
contain personally identifiable information about directors, staff,
donors, or other individuals, and sometimes sensitive discussion of
personnel, legal, or financial matters.

**Your organization controls its own privacy posture for its rendered
repository.** If this repository is public, or you are otherwise unsure
whether specific minutes are appropriate for this level of visibility,
keep minutes containing PII or sensitive deliberation in your
organization's own **private** repository instead, and reference them here
only by pointer if needed.

**Never contribute real minutes, or any other real adopted content, back
to the [Golden Records](https://github.com/US-Council/golden-records)
commons.** That repository is a public, generic template — it must never
receive real organization data (see that repository's `CONTRIBUTING.md`
leak-guard rule). This directory, in *your own* rendered repository, is
the right place for your real minutes; the commons template is not.
